rier.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp;* **Heart Disease Risk Assessment:** [X] N/A</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp;* **Cancer Staging (癌症期別):** nil</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">**Chief Complaint (主訴)**</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">traffic accident with head and chest contusion hours ago.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">**Present Illness (病史)**</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">A 60-year-old female with no significant past medical history was admitted to the hospital due to traumatic intracranial hemorrhage and left rib fractures with hemothorax following a motorcycle accident.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">According to the patient, she was involved in a motorcycle accident with a car on her way to work. She was diagnosed with intracranial hemorrhage and right rib fractures at a local hospital. Due to the hospital's inability to manage her condition, she was transferred to our facility for further evaluation and management.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">Associated symptoms included loss of consciousness. The patient denied fever, chills, chest pain, chest tightness, nausea, vomiting, or other specific complaints.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">On examination, the patient's level of consciousness was E1 VEM1 (Glasgow Coma Scale: E1 VEM1), indicating deep coma. Vital signs at the time of initial assessment in the Emergency Room were: temperature 36.6 °C, blood pressure 123/92 mmHg, pulse 138 beats per minute, respiratory rate 20 breaths per minute, and oxygen saturation 98% while breathing ambient air.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">Physical examination was notable for findings consistent with head and chest trauma. CT scan revealed left hemothorax with extravasation, requiring a chest tube insertion. The CT also confirmed traumatic subdural hemorrhage and traumatic subarachnoid hemorrhage, as well as multiple left rib fractures.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">Laboratory results showed elevated pO2 at 341.9 mmHg, decreased tCO2(P)c at 20.7 mmol/L, elevated glucose at 179 mg/dl, elevated GOT at 46 U/L, elevated CK at 203 U/L, elevated CKMB at 61.0 U/L, elevated troponin-T at 0.033 ng/ml, elevated lactate at 33.0 mg/dl, elevated WBC count at 15.51 x10^3/uL with neutrophilia (91.2%), decreased HCT at 35.8%, decreased %LYM at 4.7%, and decreased APTT at 29.4 seconds. POCT revealed potassium of 2.82 mmol/L.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">Under the impression of traumatic subdural hemorrhage, traumatic subarachnoid hemorrhage, and multiple left rib fractures with hemothorax, the patient was admitted to the hospital for further management and evaluation. She underwent right fronto-temporo-parietal craniectomy with evacuation of acute subdural hematoma, duroplasty, right external ventricular drain/ICP monitor implantation, and subgaleal drain insertion for the acute subdural hematoma. Patient was admitted to surgical intensive care unit for post op care.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">**Physical Examination (身體檢查)**</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp;* **General looking:** [X] Acutely ill-looking</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp;* **Body build:** [X] Normal</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp;* **Vital signs:**</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp; &nbsp;* BT(°C): 36.6</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp; &nbsp;* BP(mmHg): 123 / 92</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp; &nbsp;* PR(/min): 138</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp; &nbsp;* RR(/min): 19</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp; &nbsp;* Pain score: 2</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp;* **Consciousness:**</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp; &nbsp;* GCS: E1 VEM1 (Eyes: 1 Verbal: E Motor: 1)</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp;* **Extremities:**</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp; &nbsp;* Freely movable: [X] Present</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp; &nbsp;* Pitting edema: [X] Absent</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp;* **Costovertebral angle knocking tenderness:** [X] Absent</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">**Surgical Operation Note Description (手術日期及方法)**</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">| 日期 | Pre-OP Diagnosis | Post-OP Diagnosis | Surgery | Doctor | Blood Loss | Anesthesia | OP Finding |</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">| 2026-03-27 | 1. Skull defect, right FTP 2. Head injury with SDH, right FTP post craniectomy | 1. Head injury with SDH, right FTP post craniectomy, 2. Skull defect, right FTP s/p right FTP cranioplasty | 1. cranioplasty, right F-T-P with Bio-mesh | 蔣艾琛 | &lt;10mL | General | 1. skull defect 2. previous op scar |</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">| 2026-03-19 | left 3rd-9th ribs fracture with hemothorax | ditto s/p VATS left decortication and SSRF of 5-6, 8-9th ribs | Video Assisted Thoracoscopic Surgery decortication of pleura and surgical stabilization of rib fracture | 鍾政錦/曹柏? | 50mL | General | 1. Hemothorax was noted over pleural cavity, VATS decortication was done. 2. Fracture was noted at left 3rd-9th ribs, SSRF of 5-6, 8-9th ribs was done. |</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">| 2026-03-07 | acute SDH, right FTP with MLS | Acute SDH, right fronto-temporo-parietal region due to tearing of Sylvian vein s/p right craniectomy for SDH removal, duroplasty, right EVD/ICP monitor implantation | 1. Right FTP craniectomy and evacuation of acute subdural hematoma. 2. Duroplasty 3. Right EVD/ICP monitor implantation 4. Subgaleal drain insertion | 蔣艾琛 | 200mL | General | 1. Thick acute subdural hematoma associated with Sylvian vein tearing. 2. Diffuse brain contusion was seen at frontal and temporal region with hematoma. 3. Extensive brain swelling was noted. 4. ICP post craniectomy and duroplasty was 9-10mmHg |</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">**Hospital Course (住院治療經過)**</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">This 60-year-old female was admitted following a motorcycle accident with severe traumatic injuries, including a traumatic acute subdural hematoma in the right fronto-temporo-parietal region, right rib fractures (2nd-9th) with hemopneumothorax, and a traumatic left clavicle fracture. She also had a history of being a Hepatitis B virus carrier.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">Upon admission, the patient presented with a Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS) of E1 VEM1, indicating deep coma. Initial imaging revealed a traumatic subdural hemorrhage, subarachnoid hemorrhage, and intracerebral hemorrhage, along with left hemothorax and multiple left rib fractures.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">On March 7, the patient underwent an emergent right fronto-temporo-parietal craniectomy with evacuation of the acute subdural hematoma, duroplasty, right external ventricular drain (EVD)/intracranial pressure (ICP) monitor implantation, and subgaleal drain insertion. Postoperatively, she was transferred to the surgical intensive care unit for close monitoring. The ICP monitor and EVD were removed on March 12.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">For the traumatic rib fractures and hemopneumothorax, a chest tube was inserted. The patient was initially treated with Curam for lung contusion starting March 9, which was then shifted to Piperacillin/Tazobactam from March 10 to March 17 to manage potential infections. On March 19, she underwent video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery (VATS) for left decortication and surgical stabilization of rib fractures (5th-6th and 8th-9th ribs). The patient was intubated from March 7 to March 30.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">On March 27, a cranioplasty was performed to address the right fronto-temporo-parietal skull defect, utilizing a Bio-mesh for brain protection and cosmetic purposes.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">Throughout her hospitalization, her neurological status was closely monitored, and supportive care, including chest physiotherapy, was provided. By March 30, the patient's respiratory pattern was fair after extubation, and her vital signs were stable. Her GCS improved to E4M6V2, with left upper extremity muscle power of 1 and others at 4. Laboratory tests showed improving renal and liver function, though hemoglobin levels had decreased. Chest X-rays on March 30 and March 31 showed increased haziness in the left lung but clear bilateral costophrenic angles. She transferred to ordinary ward under stable condition on 2026-03-31.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">At the time of discharge, the patient's condition was stable, and she was planned for continued monitoring of neurological status, wound care, and participation in a rehabilitation program. Oxygen therapy was being tapered.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">**Complications (合併症)**</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">Pneumonia</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">**Laboratory findings (一般檢查記錄)**</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">Blood</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">**Micro-organism finding (微生物檢查)**</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">(2026-03-16) [Sputum] Culture Sputum culture (第三套), 細菌培養結果 Microorganism was isolated.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">**Discharge Status (出院時狀況)**</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp;* [X] MBD (可出院)</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp;* [X] 出院及門診追蹤</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp;* GCS improved to E4M6V2, with left upper extremity muscle power of 1 and others at 4. Respiratory pattern was smoothly under O2 mask and being tapered.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">**Discharge Medications (出院帶藥)**</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp;* Had NG for feeding and Foley inserted, plan removed Foley on 4/6</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp;* Plan tapered O2 to nasal canula</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">**Instructions on Discharge (出院指示)**</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp;* keep rehabilitation program</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">&nbsp;* sitting balance training</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">**Injury Severity Score (外傷嚴重度分數)**</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">36</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">*臺北醫學大學附設醫院 (1060720病歷管理委員會審查通過)*</font></div><div><br></div><div></div>